{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792352802,"nonce":"/Tn8EYRh37j0qzkg111YFB1aGXA=","title":"InlineFlow cannot be attached to nodes that were not made with HXX","message":"**What happens**\n\nHXX attaches `InlineFlow` only to `p`, `h1` to `h6`, `dt`, `dd`, `caption`, `legend` and `figcaption`. A host that makes nodes directly, as RayDE's Extension Studio Preview does from JSON ops with `tree.createNode()` and `Identity.register`, gets none: `\u003cp\u003ea \u003cstrong\u003eb\u003c/strong\u003e c\u003c/p\u003e` is drawn as separate boxes, the spaces at each box's edge are dropped, and it does not wrap as a paragraph.\n\nAttaching it from outside is hard for two reasons:\n- `InlineFlow.attach(root:Div)` takes a `Div` and registers `Owner.onCleanup`, so it needs an owner scope that outlives the host's own show and hide of the nodes.\n- It inserts its own anchor and spacer nodes at the front of the root's children (`replaceChildren` with `[anchor, spacer].concat(children)`), and a host that places children with `replaceChildren` drops them.\n\n**Asked for**\n\nA way to make a node a flow root from a node id and a tree, with an explicit dispose in place of `Owner.onCleanup`, and with its helper nodes kept out of the child list the host sets. Or the intended way to do it, if there is one.\n\nReported by RayDE's session (its issue 4a42535). Not scheduled.","files":null}]}